<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). Its picture (architect 2026-10-12; the baton since
     2026-10-18): the conductor's baton, the caption's icon and the glyph
     Warp wears, assets/icons/AppIcon.png (a symlink to Warp.png, 256 x 256
     since 2026-10-19), resized by ImageMagick's Lanczos filter (the GUI's
     own filter family) and centered over WHITE, FLAT (architect 2026-10-17): #FFFFFF, one color
     over the whole canvas, so the mask shows a white shape carrying the
     drawing (Windows Storm's caption start #800080 from 2026-10-16 until
     then, the Cool Edit case's 20 face-ramp bands under Midnight's Face
     from 2026-10-12 before it). An
     ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so
     no legacy ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/, BOTH RENDERED AT
     EVERY BUILD by android/app/build_apk.sh's launcher step into its staged
     copy of res/ (architect 2026-10-19: the icon follows a dropped drawing
     with no step; the Linux desktop icon is the same drawing bare, a link
     into the repository, docs/INSTALL.md):
       ic_launcher_background.png  the full 108 dp canvas flat in #FFFFFF;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the drawing rendered at the 52 dp art size,
                                   centred on a transparent canvas of the
                                   density's full 108 dp.

     THE 66 dp SAFE ZONE: an adaptive foreground's art should sit inside the
     mask's guaranteed-visible inner circle, Android's own 66 dp of the 108 dp
     canvas. The 48-unit drawing at 52 dp square (13/12 dp a unit; architect
     2026-10-16, his pick off a 60 / 56 / 52 / 48 / 44 / 40 dp series on the
     glass: at 64 dp the art filled ~86 % of the launcher's visible tile and
     nearly touched its corners). The 52 dp square's own corners
     (half-diagonal 36.8 dp) lie outside the 33 dp radius of that circle,
     but they are empty: the baton's farthest ink (its tip, toward the
     upper right corner) lies 29.1 of its 48 units, 31.5 dp, from the
     center, inside the circle with 1.5 dp to spare. The same 52 dp
     at every density (the per-density PNG pixel size scales with the density
     factor f alone):

       density  f    canvas C=108f  art 52f  offset (C-52f)/2
       mdpi     1    108            52       28
       hdpi     1.5  162            78       42
       xhdpi    2    216            104      56
       xxhdpi   3    324            156      84
       xxxhdpi  4    432            208      112

     A BUILD PRODUCT, NEVER COMMITTED: this file is the one tracked file of
     res/, and build_apk.sh writes the PNGs beside it in the package tree
     (byte-stable, -strip) from whatever drawing AppIcon.png names at the
     build. The safe-zone figure above is the baton's; a new drawing's ink
     is its own. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
